# basePath Chapter7 

::FirstContractOpenCh7
@trigger    OnContractSelectOpen
@cutscene 
@once 

//call to Keela
//ringing... while he is talking

{@Player}   Nothing. Again.
{@PAL}      You seem distracted, Captain. Time to earn some money?
{@Player}   What?...
{@Player} 	I haven't heard from her in... months. 
{@Player}	Keela's gone completely dark...
{@Player}	She could shed some light on all this for me...
{@Player}	...maybe even help Blaze and Mara. 

//no answer



::AfterDesignCh7
@trigger    OnOverarchingLoaded
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Design)
@cutscene 
@once

//call to Keela again
//ringing... while he is talking


{@Player}   What's going on with these bots? I'm worried...
{@PAL}      I'm always available to answer your questions, Captain!
{@Player}	Does she think I wrecked the ship and then sold out to Frontier?
{@Player}	I'M DOING ALL THIS TO GET MY TEAM BACK TOGETHER. 
{@Player}	Keela... I'm doing it for you guys. 

//no answer

{@PAL}		We have a contract to fulfill, Captain.  


::AfterSupplyChain
@trigger 
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Research), IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Supply)
@cutscene 
@once 

//call Keela
//ringing...
//ringing...
//no answer

{@Player}   Keela...


::AfterFabrication
@trigger
@when       IsSolutionFoundFor(Research), IsSolutionFoundFor(Design), IsSolutionFoundFor(Supply), IsSolutionFoundFor(Fabrication)
@cutscene 
@once 

//call mara 
{@Player}   Mara! How's Blaze?
{@Mara}     He's alright. Frustrated, but alright.
{@Mara}		Already prepping for the winter festival. The Long Night Festival. 
{@Player}	What's that?
{@Mara}	At dusk, everyone extinguishes their lights. An old miner's lamp is lit at the mine entrance, and people pass the light from lamp to lamp until the whole settlement is illuminated.
{@Player}   Wow, that sounds beautiful.  And the strike?
{@Mara}     People are scared, Locke. They want Frontier to guarantee the bots won't put anyone else in the hospital.
{@Player}   I've noticed it's getting riskier to source from Kalvis.
{@Mara}     But we're willing to take that risk. We need to protect our people.
//end call
